    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "This was an upfront-quoted trip (SGD 22.00) and the only sum in dispute is the separate SGD 3.20 ERP line for the Bukit Merah Central westbound gantry. That line cannot stand, and the whole contested SGD 3.20 is returned.\n\nTo the rider: you are right about the ERP line. The GPS trace for this trip is complete and unimpaired — 169 fixes at a 10-second sampling interval, 100% coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0 seconds — and the platform's own proximity check puts the car's nearest fix 7,482 m from the gantry, roughly thirty times outside the 250 m radius POL-RD-09 uses to treat a gantry as crossed. The derived block reports no bracketing gaps and gap_brackets_closest_approach false, and the fare_breakdown itself flags the gantry as on_optimal_route false. Under POL-RD-09(4) a charge for a gantry the trace never passes is a billing-integrity failure and is refunded in full. Independently, POL-RD-11(a) returns the amount by which charged_total (SGD 25.20) exceeds the quote (SGD 22.00) plus properly chargeable pass-throughs (SGD 0.00), which is the same SGD 3.20. This is one correction of SGD 3.20, not two: POL-RD-09(1)'s anti-double-count rule keeps it from being added on top of anything else, and POL-RD-02 does not run on an upfront fare, so no distance-or-time refund is available however large the excess. You are therefore recorded as entirely right on the contested amount.\n\nTo the driver: your account that you did not see or pass the gantry is consistent with the trace and supports the finding, but the deciding fact is carried by the GPS trace and fare_breakdown, both at weight 1.0. What the trace shows beyond the gantry does not change the money. The route was measured at 16.0 km against a 12.5 km optimal — an established excess of 3.5 km, 28.0%, clearing the POL-RD-01 gate — but on an UPFRONT_QUOTE fare POL-RD-11 fixes the distance and time charges at booking and no distance refund is available however large the excess. The excess is also below the materiality gate (50% or 8.0 km), so the POL-RD-06 driver_profile check is not required; in any event deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 610 completed trips in 90 days, no repeat pattern is established, and no conduct referral attaches. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-09114-01, weight 0.0) is not held against you: it could only have exculpated, it rests on no field, and its absence carries no fact.\n\nEscalation is not engaged. The single unmatched charge line is the one refunded under POL-RD-09(4), and POL-RD-09 expressly provides that POL-RD-10(8) is not triggered where the only unmatched line is refunded under that limb; the refund is far below the SGD 150.00 ceiling; trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown; and the trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a)–(c).\n\nThe SGD 3.20 is refunded in full (amount already a multiple of SGD 0.05), and the billing-integrity finding is referred as set out above."
